WEBVTT

00:16:28.984 --> 00:16:30.027
(Laughter)

00:16:30.027 --> 00:16:31.319
I'm an optimist.

00:16:31.319 --> 00:16:32.904
I’m a glass-half-full girl.

00:16:32.904 --> 00:16:35.615
So I know that we’re running out of time,

00:16:35.615 --> 00:16:37.659
time is the most precious
resource we have,

00:16:37.701 --> 00:16:39.036
and there isn't much of it.

00:16:39.077 --> 00:16:41.830
If we get this right soon,
it can really work.

00:16:41.872 --> 00:16:45.167
If we get it wrong, will be fighting
each other with sticks and stones

00:16:45.208 --> 00:16:47.669
for scraps of food and water
on an overheated planet

00:16:47.711 --> 00:16:49.963
in the ruins of dictator-world.

00:16:50.005 --> 00:16:51.256
But --

00:16:51.298 --> 00:16:52.299
(Laughter)

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:54.468
OK. But we could get it right.

00:16:54.509 --> 00:16:57.596
That’s why I feel
we’ve arrived at this moment before,

00:16:57.637 --> 00:16:59.765
and it might disappear
back into space-time.

00:16:59.806 --> 00:17:03.769
Then we'll have to wait billions of years
to get here again, which is so dull.